.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_TIMESTAMP 3 2026-09-10 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_timestamp \- set an explicit FILETIME on an MPQ file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_timestamp("
.BI "        mpq_writer_s " "*writer",
.BI "        uint64_t      " "filetime"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the timestamp of an active file writer before libmpq__writer_finish().
The archive must enable LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_FILETIME in options.attributes.
Windows FILETIME is an unsigned count of 100-nanosecond ticks since
1601-01-01 UTC, not Unix time;
zero is the default. No filesystem timestamp is imported by file_add_path.
This call neither changes the source file nor creates a patch.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS on success or a negative libmpq error.
FORMAT means FILETIME generation was not enabled.
NULL arguments return EXIST. Use on the wrong handle type returns NOT_INITIALIZED.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes_flags (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_finish (3)
